## Flags for the VM lmx runs: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here

## File names are UTF-8 whatever the locale says. Docker images, cron and
## `ssh host lmx` often run with no locale set, and the VM then fell back to
## latin1 and Elixir warned about it twice on every command.
+fnu

## The init process may spend at most this long shutting the system down
## (`System.stop/1`); then it stops whatever is left. lmx ends every command
## that way, so a stuck shutdown must not keep the command from returning.
-shutdown_time 10000
<%= if match?({:unix, _}, :os.type()) do %>
## lmx is a command, not a node an operator attaches to, so Ctrl-C must not
## open the emulator's BREAK menu ("BREAK: (a)bort (A)bort with dump
## (c)ontinue ..."), which took the terminal and left the run going until a
## second Ctrl-C. The launcher receives the interrupt and asks the VM to stop
## with SIGTERM, which cancels the running turn first (Lmx.Boot). Not on
## Windows, whose launcher runs the VM in the foreground and forwards nothing.
+Bi
<% end %>
